silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_04_negative_witnesses_decomposition_step_3__step_joc_§6_20_yoneda_embedding__full_and_faithful;_two_objects_i a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Joy of Cats §6.20 states that the Yoneda embedding is full and faithful: two objects are isomorphic exactly when their representable functors are naturally isomorphic. Showing that catus has no representable functor isomorphic to Mittens is a legitimate categorical claim. The negative witness (gippidy00 collision list) provides the evidence that Hom(catus, Mittens) is empty and thus no such natural isomorphism exists." .
